Upstream commit the port matches:
  0ac649541fca5b7a80bb724a308229fa4cfb2574   2026-11-09T22:18:40+01:00

How to port forward: diff the upstream files below against that commit (git diff 0ac6495..HEAD -- dll/ai/<file>)
and carry the changed decisions into the Lua module named. The port keeps the decisions (budgets, targets, timings,
the force's rules), not the engine patches: what upstream patches into the original exe (danger routes, honest
vision, the group move, the unload retries) is a C++ helper of this engine (docs/AI_LUA_UNITS.md §4, §11).

Per-file map (upstream dll/ai/<file> -> this folder):
  econ.c        budget_reserve / spend_reserve (the epoch reserve), hook_add_resource (the military account and its
                income shares), econ_targets (the worker plan by shortfall and rate), citizens_home (not ported:
                the engine's finders keep citizens on safe sites), gather_research, early_requirements, the copper
                plan's epoch attempt, substitute_soldier (the strongest affordable soldier), hoard caps
                                                                        -> econ.lua (budget, workers, epoch), army.lua (choice)
  early.c       early_towers (two towers by the town centre: the front and the citizens' side), the builders
                                                                        -> econ.lua (towers); tower_bait, early_militia: the
                                                                           engine's reflexes (ai.reflex on) stand in
  food.c        food_plan_needs (the citizens' food, the real wood need), the hunters       -> econ.lua (workers)
  mines.c       mine_drops / wood_drops (a settlement at the unworked mine or forest edge nearest a drop site)
                                                                        -> econ.lua (settlements)
  citizens.c    cz_targets (the citizens wanted from the mines' places, FEED)                -> econ.lua (citizens)
  defence.c     def_refresh (the fronts: towards the nearest enemy buildings known), defence_tick (towers at the
                fronts and the outposts), home_guard, muster                            -> econ.lua (towers), army.lua
  armies.c      the force (one land army ordered as one: home at the station, the push at the attack time when it
                beats the enemy at the target by AR_GO_PCT, the judge every AR_JUDGE_EVERY, home under AR_BACK_PCT
                twice running, the next building, the raid answered, the way home as a convoy)   -> army.lua
  stage.c       the staging point (the last point of the way out of the enemy's reach)       -> army.lua
  intel.c       honest vision's memory (buildings until seen gone, soldiers remembered 3 minutes)
                                                                        -> C++: the enemy memory (ai.memory)
  danger.c      the threat map (defences at range, soldiers, hurt citizens)           -> C++: ai.danger "threat"
  cover.c       DANGER_LOST (where own units traded badly, 20 minutes)                 -> C++: ai.danger "lost"
  shiproute.c   danger-aware routes                                                     -> C++: ai.route (cells)
  army.c        army_plan BUILD (one more production building of the kind trained when the producers are busy)
                                                                        -> econ.lua (buildings)
  Not ported yet (in order of value): landing.c, fleet.c, navy.c, transports.c (the navy and landings), expand.c,
  towns.c (other islands, resource towns, forward bases), attack.c (siege, weak spots, the commander's patches),
  bunker.c, garrison.c (garrison upgrades), counterfire.c, airstrike.c, diplo.c, spoils.c, skirmish.c, metal.c,
  mass.c, fronts.c, sites.c, packing.c, priority.c, forces.c, stats.c.

Settings: settings.lua carries the [ai_base] defaults of config/ageofai.ini at that commit, with the deviations
noted there (epoch pacing: the port advances as soon as the epoch is paid, upstream's "independent" timer of 50-70
minutes an epoch is for games of 200-400 population a player).
